      "text": [
        " سُئِلَ عَنِ الرَّجُلِ يُقْسِمُ عَلَى أَخِيهِ قَالَ لَيْسَ عَلَيْهِ شَيْ‏ءٌ إِنَّمَا أَرَادَ إِكْرَامَهُ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ahmad Bin Muhammad, from Ibn Fazzal, from Hafs, and someone else from our companions, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup>, said, ‘He<sup>asws</sup> was asked about the man who swore upon his brother. He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘There is nothing upon him. But rather he intended to honour him’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "12. Ahmad ibn Muhammad has narrated from ibn Faddal from Hafs and from more than one person of our people who has narrated the following: “Once abu ‘ Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, was asked about the case of a man who swears by his brother. He (the Imam) said, ‘It does not have any valid effect on him; he only wanted to honor and respect him.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
